# Demo Show Code

A developer copies Show Code and uses it. That is the only job of the snippet.

- Every Show Code calls the component it documents, with the real props. Do not stop at a comment, a `triggerNotification({...})` payload, or a class string cut off with `...`.
- Visible text goes through `t()`. Do not hardcode titles, labels, descriptions, button copy, or alt text in the demo template or in Show Code.
- Use the feature `t()` key when one exists. If the source file still has a raw English string, add a feature key and call `t()` in the demo anyway.
- A Show Code `t()` path never starts with `demo.`. That namespace is only for the demo page's own chrome (section titles, captions). A developer pastes the snippet into a real page.
- File-name captions above a sample are not part of the component. Do not print them as hardcoded text.
- Do not wrap DemoPage component sections in dark/demo stage backgrounds (`bg-[#272727]`, fake panels, etc.). Show the component on the page as-is.
- Do not add DemoPage samples into feature/product sections — demos live only under `demo-audit` / DemoPage.
